
1. map() — Transform every element

map() creates a new array by applying a function to every element.

const doubled = numbers.map((num) => {
    return num * 2;
});

console.log(doubled);

Output:

[2, 4, 6, 8, 10]

Think:

map → "Change every element"

2. filter() — Select elements

filter() creates a new array containing only the elements that satisfy a condition.

const evenNumbers = numbers.filter((num) => {
    return num % 2 === 0;
});

console.log(evenNumbers);

Output:

[2, 4]

Think:

filter → "Keep only the elements I want"

3. Reduce is an array method that processes each element and accumulates the result into a single final value.
